    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI would like to use dir.lua as a temporary viewport/browser. The documented autocmd mostly accomplishes that:\n`autocmd FileType directory setlocal bufhidden=delete`\n\nHowever, I also do not want the alternate file to be set for dir buffers.\n\nCurrently (with the above autocmd):\n1. I am on buffer A\n2. Open dir browser (`-`)\n3. Open buffer B\n4. `ctrl-^` brings me to the dir buffer\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. I am on buffer A\n2. Open dir browser (`-`)\n3. Open buffer B\n4. `ctrl-^` brings me to buffer A",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-05T17:37:00Z",
    "closed_by": {
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}",
