        "user_view_type": "public"
    },
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The linked #41014 does not resolve your issue. Something like this does:\n\n```lua\nlocal alt\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n  pattern = 'directory',\n  callback = function() alt = vim.fn.bufnr('#') end,\n})\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('BufEnter', {\n  callback = function(args)\n    if alt and vim.bo[args.buf].filetype ~= 'directory' then\n      vim.cmd.balt(vim.fn.bufname(alt))\n      alt = nil\n    end\n  end,\n})\n```\n@justinmk pushed (and, for the record, **I implemented**, because I think it makes sense XD) for directory buffers to be treated like \"normal,\" including respecting alternative buffers. The way to get around this is to set a bufhidden setting, but that has consequences (which I further clarified in the linked pr), including wiping the alternative buffer.\n\nSo, if you seek this \"abnormal\" behavior, you can use the snippet above. I'm not sure what the general consensus on what most people would expect here, but I only want to introduce new buffer semantics if it's truly desirable. Would appreciate some clarity from @justinmk here, including whether to include the above recipe in the linked pr. ",
            "created_at": "2026-07-27T20:34:17Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41004#issuecomment-5096513619",
