        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "If wanting directory buffers to be treated as temporary buffers is wrong and abnormal, then neither this recipe nor the existing `bufhidden` autocmd should be documented IMO. Anybody who wants to use the existing autocmd probably wants the alternate file to be preserved too.\n\nDirectory buffers are not modifiable and they feel different then my normal files I'm editing. So I only want `ctrl-^`, `ctrl-o`, etc to bring me to the stuff I'm editing.",
