        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@justinmk](https://github.com/justinmk) pushed for directory buffers to be treated like \"normal,\"\n\nThat is a useful guiding principle, but it doesn't necessarily mean every aspect needs to be exactly like a normal buffer.\n\nvim-dirvish tries to reach for that, but also tries to preserve the alt-buf. However it can be tricky to get right. Storing `w:dirvish.altbuf` is a decent approach, but the tricky part is deciding when to restore the alt-buf.",
